WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.803 --> 00:00:03.105
everyone is wondering is why.

00:00:03.238 --> 00:00:03.639
Why?

00:00:03.639 --> 00:00:04.340
Hopefully they'll get to the

00:00:04.473 --> 00:00:06.542
bottom of it.

00:00:06.675 --> 00:00:07.209
Thank you very much.

00:00:07.643 --> 00:00:08.744
&gt;&gt;&gt; Look at this picture that we

00:00:08.877 --> 00:00:10.479
have from the Michigan state

00:00:10.612 --> 00:00:12.147
campus in the hours after the

00:00:12.281 --> 00:00:12.648
shooting.

00:00:12.648 --> 00:00:13.649
You can see that young man there

00:00:13.782 --> 00:00:14.750
highlighted on the right side of

00:00:14.883 --> 00:00:15.651
the screen.

00:00:15.651 --> 00:00:18.020
He is wearing an oxford strong

00:00:18.153 --> 00:00:18.921
sweatshirt.

00:00:19.054 --> 00:00:19.755
Oxford, that's in reference to

00:00:19.888 --> 00:00:20.388
high school.

00:00:20.489 --> 00:00:22.224
That is near Detroit.

00:00:22.358 --> 00:00:25.661
As many of you know, a gunman

00:00:25.761 --> 00:00:27.796
killed four students and wounded

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.698
seven other people just 15

00:00:29.832 --> 00:00:30.232
months ago.

00:00:30.232 --> 00:00:31.667
That student says he got the

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:33.235
t-shirt at a fund-raiser but

00:00:33.669 --> 00:00:34.870
underscores the reality that she

00:00:35.004 --> 00:00:36.105
is referencing there that some

00:00:36.238 --> 00:00:37.673
of the people, some of the

00:00:37.673 --> 00:00:39.675
students survived not one but

00:00:39.675 --> 00:00:42.244
two mass shootings.

00:00:42.378 --> 00:00:43.812
&gt;&gt; For me, the most haunting

00:00:43.946 --> 00:00:45.681
picture of last night was

00:00:45.714 --> 00:00:47.249
watching the cameras pan through

00:00:47.683 --> 00:00:49.885
the crowds and seeing a young

00:00:50.019 --> 00:00:52.521
person wearing an oxford strong

00:00:52.654 --> 00:00:53.055
sweatshirt.

00:00:53.055 --> 00:00:54.990
The sweatshirts handed out after

00:00:55.124 --> 00:00:56.158
those kids lived through a

00:00:56.291 --> 00:00:57.860
school shooting 15 months ago.

00:00:57.993 --> 00:00:59.194
And we have children in Michigan

00:00:59.328 --> 00:01:01.697
who are living through their

00:01:01.697 --> 00:01:02.564
second school shooting in under

00:01:02.698 --> 00:01:05.100
a year and a half.

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:06.602
&gt;&gt; Joining us now is one of

00:01:06.735 --> 00:01:08.303
those students, a student

00:01:08.437 --> 00:01:09.204
traumatized by the mass

00:01:09.338 --> 00:01:10.773
shootings at Michigan state and

00:01:10.906 --> 00:01:13.709
at her high school, oxford high

00:01:13.809 --> 00:01:15.144
school, Eva Ferguson.

00:01:15.277 --> 00:01:16.311
I'm so glad you're here with us

00:01:16.445 --> 00:01:16.912
this morning.

00:01:16.912 --> 00:01:17.880
You're so young.

00:01:18.013 --> 00:01:19.181
You're my little brother's age.

00:01:19.314 --> 00:01:21.350
He's a freshman in college.

00:01:21.717 --> 00:01:24.553
And I know you had been --

00:01:24.686 --> 00:01:25.754
oxford high school was your high

00:01:25.888 --> 00:01:26.221
school.

00:01:26.221 --> 00:01:29.058
You've been on this campus for

00:01:29.191 --> 00:01:29.792
weeks and now another shooting

00:01:29.925 --> 00:01:30.359
has happened.

00:01:30.359 --> 00:01:33.829
What was going through your

00:01:33.962 --> 00:01:34.462
mind?

00:01:34.563 --> 00:01:37.733
&gt;&gt; I was flabbergasted to say

00:01:37.733 --> 00:01:38.734
the least.

00:01:38.867 --> 00:01:40.936
After oxford, they said that

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.204
this wasn't going to happen

00:01:42.337 --> 00:01:42.837
again.

00:01:42.838 --> 00:01:44.273
We were going to be safe going

00:01:44.406 --> 00:01:45.274
back to school.

00:01:45.407 --> 00:01:49.178
And that's just not the case.

00:01:49.311 --> 00:01:51.113
The other night I was in shock.

00:01:51.246 --> 00:01:54.383
I didn't think it was real,

00:01:54.516 --> 00:01:54.883
honestly.

00:01:54.883 --> 00:02:00.122
&gt;&gt; Did you know any of the

00:02:00.255 --> 00:02:00.589
victims?

00:02:00.589 --> 00:02:04.626
&gt;&gt; At oxford, I did nomad I son

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:07.763
-- know Madison but at msu I

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:08.464
didn't know any of them.

00:02:08.597 --> 00:02:09.965
&gt;&gt; Were there similarities to

00:02:10.099 --> 00:02:10.999
how you were alerted?

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:12.167
Did you get anything from the

00:02:12.301 --> 00:02:12.634
school?

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:13.769
Was there a mass alert or

00:02:13.802 --> 00:02:15.971
anything that went out?

00:02:16.105 --> 00:02:18.140
&gt;&gt; There was an e-mail that went

00:02:18.273 --> 00:02:20.342
out to a lot of the students who

00:02:20.476 --> 00:02:25.314
had signed up for the safe msu

00:02:25.447 --> 00:02:25.781
app.

00:02:25.781 --> 00:02:29.785
&gt;&gt; Eva, what is it like to be on

00:02:29.918 --> 00:02:31.286
campus, to have to call your

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:33.021
parents again to talk about the

00:02:33.155 --> 00:02:34.256
message that's you're getting

00:02:34.389 --> 00:02:35.290
from officials, what you're

00:02:35.424 --> 00:02:36.658
seeing on social media and

00:02:36.792 --> 00:02:37.893
hearing from friends about the

00:02:38.026 --> 00:02:42.631
cop cars that were on campus?

00:02:42.764 --> 00:02:51.807
&gt;&gt; It was like traumatizing all

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:52.341
over again.

00:02:52.341 --> 00:02:53.475
At the time we didn't know

00:02:53.809 --> 00:02:55.811
information.
I didn't know where the shooter

00:02:55.811 --> 00:02:56.211
was.

00:02:56.211 --> 00:03:00.616
I thought I was in imminent

00:03:00.749 --> 00:03:02.050
danger.

00:03:02.184 --> 00:03:02.618
Yeah.

00:03:02.618 --> 00:03:03.385
It was horrifying.

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:07.022
&gt;&gt; You are going to see someone?

00:03:07.156 --> 00:03:08.590
-- Are you going to see someone?

00:03:08.724 --> 00:03:09.224
&gt;&gt; Pardon?

00:03:09.291 --> 00:03:10.526
&gt;&gt; Are you going to see someone

00:03:10.659 --> 00:03:12.628
or talk to someone like a

00:03:12.761 --> 00:03:13.162
counsellor?

00:03:13.162 --> 00:03:13.495
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:03:13.495 --> 00:03:15.831
After oxford I was going to a

00:03:15.831 --> 00:03:16.999
therapist for a while.

00:03:17.132 --> 00:03:18.100
And then I stopped.

00:03:18.233 --> 00:03:20.936
But right now I actually am

00:03:21.069 --> 00:03:22.237
seeing a therapist.

00:03:22.371 --> 00:03:23.272
&gt;&gt; You are.

00:03:23.405 --> 00:03:24.706
Listen, this is what the text

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:26.975
message from the school said.

00:03:27.109 --> 00:03:30.045
The protocol, I think is run,

00:03:30.179 --> 00:03:30.812
hide, and fight.

00:03:30.946 --> 00:03:32.014
What do you think of that

00:03:32.147 --> 00:03:32.647
guidance?

00:03:32.648 --> 00:03:35.851
There were people in a classroom

00:03:35.884 --> 00:03:36.818
and someone knocking on the

00:03:36.952 --> 00:03:38.587
door.
They didn't know if it was

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:39.220
police or not.

00:03:39.288 --> 00:03:40.556
What do you think of the

00:03:40.689 --> 00:03:42.057
guidance you got and getting

00:03:42.191 --> 00:03:47.996
from these -- in these

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:48.530
situations?

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:51.300
&gt;&gt; I think that those are

00:03:51.433 --> 00:03:56.271
very -- like -- what's the word?

00:03:56.405 --> 00:03:57.973
Understandable, good things you

00:03:58.106 --> 00:03:58.707
should be doing.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:03:59.875
It's important to not shut down

00:03:59.975 --> 00:04:02.077
and to save yourself.

00:04:02.211 --> 00:04:04.213
And to fight for everyone around

00:04:04.346 --> 00:04:08.050
you and not let someone like

00:04:08.183 --> 00:04:10.485
that get what they want

00:04:10.619 --> 00:04:11.019
essentially.

00:04:11.019 --> 00:04:12.654
&gt;&gt; I just want to talk about how

00:04:12.788 --> 00:04:13.889
amazing you are and what you've

00:04:13.889 --> 00:04:14.389
been through.

00:04:14.456 --> 00:04:15.290
Not only did you have the

00:04:15.424 --> 00:04:17.159
shooting at your high school and

00:04:17.292 --> 00:04:18.627
you just experienced this one at

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:19.895
Michigan state, you're also a

00:04:19.962 --> 00:04:21.330
cancer survivor.

00:04:21.463 --> 00:04:23.031
You had only been at campus a

00:04:23.165 --> 00:04:24.132
few weeks.

00:04:24.266 --> 00:04:25.367
This is supposed to be one of

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:26.568
the most exciting times in your

00:04:26.702 --> 00:04:27.903
life, you're going to college.

00:04:27.903 --> 00:04:28.704
You have this big moment.

00:04:28.837 --> 00:04:31.206
You accomplished that.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:33.909
Do you feel like the system

00:04:34.042 --> 00:04:35.244
failed you given that this

00:04:35.377 --> 00:04:36.478
happened to you twice?

00:04:36.612 --> 00:04:39.915
&gt;&gt; 100%.

00:04:39.915 --> 00:04:42.818
There should have been laws made

00:04:42.951 --> 00:04:43.919
years ago when sandy hook

00:04:44.052 --> 00:04:45.520
happened and it never did.

00:04:45.921 --> 00:04:47.155
I feel like now's the time

00:04:47.289 --> 00:04:49.491
people need to start realizing

00:04:49.925 --> 00:04:51.927
there is people dying every day

00:04:51.927 --> 00:04:53.462
because of gun violence.

00:04:53.595 --> 00:04:55.998
And something needs to be done

00:04:56.131 --> 00:04:57.432
about it.

00:04:57.566 --> 00:04:58.267
&gt;&gt; Absolutely.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:04:59.935
Eva, you are really brave.

00:04:59.968 --> 00:05:01.103
We're really glad you came on to

00:05:01.236 --> 00:05:01.937
talk about this.

00:05:01.937 --> 00:05:03.505
You're right, it's unfair you've

00:05:03.939 --> 00:05:05.073
gone through this and no one

00:05:05.207 --> 00:05:05.941
your age should have to go

00:05:06.074 --> 00:05:08.377
through this.

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:08.944
No one should.

00:05:08.944 --> 00:05:09.945
We're very glad you came on to

00:05:10.012 --> 00:05:10.646
talk about it though.

00:05:10.779 --> 00:05:12.914
&gt;&gt; Thank you for having me.

00:05:13.048 --> 00:05:13.515
&gt;&gt; Thank you.

00:05:13.515 --> 00:05:14.015
&gt;&gt; Thank you.

00:05:14.016 --> 00:05:15.217
Not once but twice.

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:16.585
And she's not the only one.

00:05:16.718 --> 00:05:18.053
There are others who have gone

00:05:18.186 --> 00:05:20.656
through it more than once.

00:05:20.789 --> 00:05:21.556
Look, I can't imagine what I

00:05:21.957 --> 00:05:22.924
would do in this situation.

00:05:23.058 --> 00:05:24.459
We were asking each other if

00:05:24.593 --> 00:05:25.961
you -- would you open the door

00:05:26.028 --> 00:05:27.529
if there was a knock and they

00:05:27.963 --> 00:05:28.964
said it is police, let me in.

00:05:29.097 --> 00:05:30.098
I don't think I would trust.

00:05:30.232 --> 00:05:31.033
That even though they may there

00:05:31.166 --> 00:05:31.967
be to save me.

00:05:31.967 --> 00:05:32.534
I don't know.

00:05:32.668 --> 00:05:33.969
I can't imagine being in that

00:05:33.969 --> 00:05:35.170
situation.
&gt;&gt; She's so young.

00:05:35.304 --> 00:05:37.172
My little brother just turned

00:05:37.306 --> 00:05:39.308
19.
&gt;&gt; Do they talk about it?

00:05:39.441 --> 00:05:40.776
&gt;&gt; It's just what they've grown

00:05:40.909 --> 00:05:41.376
up with.

00:05:41.376 --> 00:05:42.744
And they do get that training.

00:05:42.878 --> 00:05:44.179
The fact she's been through it

00:05:44.313 --> 00:05:44.746
before.

00:05:44.746 --> 00:05:46.248
But to hear her dad talking to

00:05:46.381 --> 00:05:47.983
Allison last night and saying we

00:05:47.983 --> 00:05:49.985
just couldn't believe that you

